subproblems.statement:
Let P, m ∈ ℕ, write ℝ^k = Euclid k with the Euclidean norm |·|, and let G : ℝ^m → ℝ^P be of class C¹ (ContDiff ℝ 1 G). Let x ∈ ℝ^m be a point at which the derivative DG(x) = fderiv ℝ G x : ℝ^m → ℝ^P is injective. Then there is r > 0 with two properties:
- G is injective on the closed ball B̄_r(x) = {z : |z − x| ≤ r};
- DG(z) is injective for every z ∈ B̄_r(x).

Let P, m ∈ ℕ, let G : ℝ^m → ℝ^P be of class C¹ (ContDiff ℝ 1 G; ℝ^k = Euclid k), x ∈ ℝ^m and r ∈ ℝ. Assume:
- G is injective on the closed ball B̄_r(x) = {z : |z − x| ≤ r};
- DG(z) = fderiv ℝ G z is injective for every z in the open ball B_r(x) = {z : |z − x| < r}.
Then N := G(B_r(x)) is an embedded m-dimensional C¹ submanifold of ℝ^P in the sense of the contract (IsEmbeddedSubmanifold 1 m N). That is, every y ∈ N has an open W ∋ y, an open V ⊆ ℝ^m and a map ψ such that:
- ψ is C¹ on V and injective on V;
- ψ(V) = W ∩ N;
- V ∩ ψ⁻¹(K) is compact for every compact K ⊆ W;
- Dψ(z) is injective for every z ∈ V.
If r ≤ 0, then N = ∅ and the statement is vacuous.

Let P, m ∈ ℕ and let G : ℝ^m → ℝ^P be of class C¹ (ContDiff ℝ 1 G; ℝ^k = Euclid k). Then there are:
- a set N₀ ⊆ ℝ^P with H^m(N₀) = 0 (H^m = μHE[m]);
- sets N_l ⊆ ℝ^P (l ∈ ℕ), each an embedded m-dimensional C¹ submanifold of ℝ^P in the sense of the contract (IsEmbeddedSubmanifold 1 m N_l);
such that G(ℝ^m) ⊆ N₀ ∪ ⋃_l N_l.
